{title: One Day}
{artist: J. Wilbur Chapman & Charles Marsh}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 84}

Verse 1
[Bb]One day when heaven was [Eb]filled with his praises, [Bb]one day when sin was as [F]black as could be,
[Bb]Jesus came forth to be [Eb]born of a virgin, [Bb]dwelt among men, my ex[F]ample is [Bb]he!

Chorus
[Bb]Living, he loved me; [Eb]dying, he saved me; [Bb]buried, he carried my [F]sins far away;
[Bb]rising, he justified [Eb]freely forever: [Bb]one day he's coming — O [F]glorious [Bb]day!
